{"id": "EUVD-2026-59209", "enisaUuid": "bed77100-628a-3bc6-90cd-12c7e5f33363", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nsmb: client: fix overflow in passthrough ioctl bounds check\n\nsmb2_ioctl_query_info() validates the PASSTHRU_FSCTL response payload\nbefore copying it to userspace.\n\nThe payload offset and length both come from 32-bit fields. The bounds\ncheck currently adds OutputOffset and qi.input_buffer_length directly, so\nthe addition can wrap in 32-bit arithmetic before the result is compared\nagainst the response buffer length.\n\nA malicious server can use a large OutputOffset and a small OutputCount\nto make the wrapped sum pass the bounds check. The later copy_to_user()\nthen reads from io_rsp + OutputOffset, outside the response buffer.\n\nUse size_add() for the offset plus length check so overflow is treated as\nout of bounds.", "datePublished": "2026-08-15T05:55:26", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-16T18:55:16", "baseScore": 8.1, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:N/AC:L/PR:L/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/175357ee0c596cb82054650dfa32fda51ad35aaa", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/dbd126539c098dba3159ce7d34b10b2daddcbd0f", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/63feb687e89a3a52a31e6e01764117cc500f1974", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/160045fc943f6c46b227644261252c8a22b8a87a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b30771b69eafae750afb7385fbcc3d77ed3f3670", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1627e7d5c9b09721a141d07cedb178882f1ded67", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/1a638c55f2db6cb2296e5e3138015dd8fd9d4aa9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a4f27ad055392fa164f5649e89a3637b033c5fcc"], "aliases": ["GHSA-h4wv-r484-2rg5", "CVE-2026-72310"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.64, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "13ffe5f4-7e17-31dd-80ac-99c0167b1923", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "1766068d-bf42-30dd-a7dc-b29bf797d1b1", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b1116bbe898aefdf584838448c6869f69851e0f <a4f27ad055392fa164f5649e89a3637b033c5fcc"}, {"id": "2f46bec5-6872-3c86-970c-78b665143736", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.40"}, {"id": "2f6bd007-4741-3901-b133-e1f3b1762e38", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b1116bbe898aefdf584838448c6869f69851e0f <b30771b69eafae750afb7385fbcc3d77ed3f3670"}, {"id": "536dfd1d-9f19-3e78-93d5-adcd7e7de710", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b1116bbe898aefdf584838448c6869f69851e0f <160045fc943f6c46b227644261252c8a22b8a87a"}, {"id": "552707b8-3482-39ab-b56e-746759d6d575", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b1116bbe898aefdf584838448c6869f69851e0f <dbd126539c098dba3159ce7d34b10b2daddcbd0f"}, {"id": "5ba2cf15-d35e-3deb-9a20-5b305761bb0f", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.97"}, {"id": "8c43c251-48a7-3f26-86f0-f3bf504b8383", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.145"}, {"id": "a1ce523a-5fa7-349d-a33f-7db8ab0037ae", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b1116bbe898aefdf584838448c6869f69851e0f <1a638c55f2db6cb2296e5e3138015dd8fd9d4aa9"}, {"id": "a223a89a-e351-3dc2-9c46-88d2bc5accd2", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2005c32ec99ee2490e8131b3953f3f212009ffea"}, {"id": "a38b6d8f-f708-3cc4-892e-d3f4b050a58e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "2b1116bbe898aefdf584838448c6869f69851e0f <63feb687e89a3a52a31e6e01764117cc500f1974"}, {"id": "bc9efbec-5bd3-354b-b23e-91d2c52c03ef", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2"}, {"id": "bf817de1-076a-